// Raft's commit rule (§5.3, §5.4.2): the leader of term T commits index I once a majority (itself and one of the two
// others) holds the entry and the entry was created in term T; earlier entries are committed with it.
// Blossom golden corpus, re-derived; see ../../README.md.

committed_upto(L, I) :- leading(L), leads(L, T), log(L, I, T, V), copies(L, T, I, F);
